1
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:14,630
Some things cannot be stopped.

2
00:00:14,630 --> 00:00:17,540
The tides of time,

3
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:20,370
humanity's dreams and inherited will...

4
00:00:20,370 --> 00:00:23,480
As long as people seek freedom,

5
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:26,110
these things will never cease to be.

6
00:01:50,210 --> 00:01:55,880
Straight Ahead!!

7
00:01:56,190 --> 00:01:58,470
Whoa! Look! 
Behind him!

8
00:01:58,470 --> 00:02:00,550
A rainbow! There's a rainbow!

9
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:12,480
Even his tears are gigantic!

10
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:14,570
It's practically a waterfall!

11
00:02:14,570 --> 00:02:18,030
I understand how you feel, 
Master Brogy!

12
00:02:41,890 --> 00:02:44,350
Dorry! How are you–

13
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:48,770
It seems I blacked out.

14
00:02:51,420 --> 00:02:53,610
Mr. 0?

15
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:56,300
Wasn't Mr. 0 the name

16
00:02:56,300 --> 00:02:59,570
of the enemy boss Vivi-chan mentioned?

17
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:04,530
Which means the guy on the other 
end of this transponder snail...

18
00:03:09,870 --> 00:03:12,630
is one of the
Seven Warlords of the Sea?!

19
00:03:12,630 --> 00:03:16,410
I issued your orders several days ago.

20
00:03:16,410 --> 00:03:18,460
What's taking so long?

21
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:23,430
It says "Mr. 3." So he's the owner 
of this transponder snail?

22
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:27,320
I think I got it figured out now.

23
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:29,020
This is an enemy hideout,

24
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:33,930
and a guy named Mr. 3 came 
to the island to take Vivi-chan's life.

25
00:03:34,810 --> 00:03:39,600
Dammit! I wasted
all this time on hunting!

26
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:41,930
I hope everyone's okay!

27
00:03:43,070 --> 00:03:45,660
Why the silent treatment?

28
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:48,340
I asked you a question.

29
00:03:48,340 --> 00:03:52,210
Have you eliminated Princess Vivi 
and the Straw Hats?!

30
00:03:52,210 --> 00:03:55,130
Yeah, mission complete!

31
00:03:55,130 --> 00:03:59,720
I got rid of everyone 
who knew your secret.

32
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:02,170
So there's no need 
to go after 'em anymore.

33
00:04:02,170 --> 00:04:04,300
I see. Well done.

34
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:08,200
As we speak, the Unluckies 
are headed your way

35
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:12,270
to confirm your mission is complete 
and to deliver a certain package.

36
00:04:12,270 --> 00:04:15,100
Unluckies? Package?

37
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:19,240
An eternal pose that points 
to the Kingdom of Arabasta.

38
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:27,280
You and Miss Golden Week will head 
to Arabasta. The time has come.

39
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:31,550
We will commence with our 
most critical operation to date.

40
00:04:31,550 --> 00:04:35,210
Once in Arabasta, 
await further orders.

41
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:40,630
Who the hell are these guys?!

42
00:04:49,850 --> 00:04:51,640
Hey. What's the problem?

43
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:54,100
N-No worries, it's noth–

44
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:59,110
What the hell?!

45
00:05:14,750 --> 00:05:19,400
You wanna kill me?! 
Bring it on, you damn monkey!

46
00:05:25,590 --> 00:05:27,630
I'm tellin' you...

47
00:05:30,850 --> 00:05:33,140
to cut that out,

48
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:35,810
you overgrown chicken!

49
00:05:40,810 --> 00:05:43,350
What was that?! What happened?!

50
00:05:43,350 --> 00:05:47,490
Oh, i-it's nothing. Nothing at all.

51
00:05:47,490 --> 00:05:50,450
That damn Straw Hat was still alive.

52
00:05:50,450 --> 00:05:53,090
It's okay, though. I finished him off.

53
00:05:53,090 --> 00:05:54,560
No need to worry.

54
00:05:56,370 --> 00:05:59,140
Still alive?

55
00:05:59,140 --> 00:06:02,640
You told me 
your mission was complete.

56
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:04,650
Didn't you?

57
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:08,060
Well, yes.

58
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:10,800
I thought it was, y'know?

59
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:15,020
But he was a lot tougher 
than he let on.

60
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:21,310
In other words, what you 
gave me was a false report.

61
00:06:21,310 --> 00:06:26,490
Um, well... I suppose 
that's what it sounds like.

62
00:06:26,490 --> 00:06:29,600
But! I stamped him out 
for good now.

63
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:32,530
So, no need to send anyone else. Okay?

64
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:34,410
Enough.

65
00:06:34,410 --> 00:06:39,500
You're to head straight 
to Arabasta immediately!

66
00:06:42,580 --> 00:06:46,090
It must've been... 
due to the weapons.

67
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:50,430
The weapons?! Of course!

68
00:06:51,090 --> 00:06:54,090
These weapons, 
though forged in Elbaf,

69
00:06:54,090 --> 00:06:58,430
are completely worn out after a 
century-long duel between giants!

70
00:06:59,770 --> 00:07:02,040
Of all the crazy luck.

71
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:03,610
What a miracle!

72
00:07:05,410 --> 00:07:09,570
Hey, Brogy! Don't clutch me! 
It upsets my wounds!

73
00:07:09,570 --> 00:07:12,980
I'm overjoyed you're alive, old friend!

74
00:07:18,190 --> 00:07:21,500
What miracle? 
This was bound to happen.

75
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:24,020
What's crazy is those 
weapons remain intact

76
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:26,330
despite the punishment they took.

77
00:07:26,330 --> 00:07:28,010
Not to mention their owners.

78
00:07:28,010 --> 00:07:33,470
This is truly a glorious day! 
I give thanks to the gods of Elbaf!

79
00:07:33,470 --> 00:07:35,300
Oh, Brogy?

80
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:41,390
So cutting me down and taking 
me out was a joyous occasion?

81
00:07:41,390 --> 00:07:45,020
You dimwit! 
You have the wrong idea!

82
00:07:45,020 --> 00:07:49,490
Ouch! Watch out for my wounds!

83
00:07:57,910 --> 00:07:59,660
You want some more?!

84
00:07:59,660 --> 00:08:03,240
Yeah! I'll drop you again!

85
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:09,210
Cool! Cool! Cool!

86
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:12,670
Why are you guys at it again?!

87
00:08:13,210 --> 00:08:17,180
And you will practice 
strict radio silence.

88
00:08:17,180 --> 00:08:20,640
It'll keep the Navy 
from catching on to us.

89
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:25,730
From here on, you'll only receive 
written orders, as in the past.

90
00:08:25,730 --> 00:08:29,610
That is all. Good luck, Mr. 3.

91
00:08:37,670 --> 00:08:39,910
Miss All-Sunday.

92
00:08:41,540 --> 00:08:42,620
Yes?

93
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:46,120
Have Mr. 2 stop by Little Garden.

94
00:08:47,420 --> 00:08:53,380
On his way to Arabasta from Little Garden, Mr. 3 needs to disappear.

95
00:08:53,380 --> 00:08:58,350
How cold-blooded of you, Sir "Mr. 0" Crocodile.

96
00:08:58,350 --> 00:09:03,700
We have enough manpower as it is. 
Is there a problem here?

97
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:07,940
Hm? No problem. I'll make it happen.

98
00:09:20,750 --> 00:09:23,660
Well, he hung up. So, let's see...

99
00:09:23,660 --> 00:09:27,040
Just who were these guys?

100
00:09:33,230 --> 00:09:34,760
What's this?

101
00:09:36,100 --> 00:09:38,580
Captain Smoker. Captain Smoker!

102
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:40,720
We intercepted 
an intriguing transmission.

103
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:42,220
What?

104
00:09:45,290 --> 00:09:47,850
What an incredible full temper!

105
00:09:47,850 --> 00:09:49,900
The great wazamono blade, Kashu!

106
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:52,690
Tashigi! Hey! Tashigi!

107
00:09:52,690 --> 00:09:57,900
Only on the Grand Line can you 
find a named blade so readily!

108
00:09:57,900 --> 00:09:59,280
Tashigi! Hey!

109
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:01,330
Are you deaf, you sword freak?!

110
00:10:01,330 --> 00:10:04,240
Y-Yes, sir! What is it,
Captain Smoker?! The coffee is–

111
00:10:09,610 --> 00:10:13,170
Just get over here and listen to this!

112
00:10:14,650 --> 00:10:18,340
That's a black wiretapper snail!

113
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:18,340
Black Wiretapper Snail

114
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:22,400
Listen close. We just picked up 
this conversation between two men.

115
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:24,600
Ready, Chief? 
Let's play it back.

116
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:26,810
Y-Yes. If you would.

117
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:30,020
...'s me. Mr. 0.

118
00:10:30,020 --> 00:10:33,770
Princess Vivi and the Straw Ha...

119
00:10:33,770 --> 00:10:36,030
Straw Ha...? The Straw Hat Pirates!

120
00:10:36,030 --> 00:10:39,400
Yeah, mission complete!

121
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:43,410
... you'll only... written 
orders, as in the past.

122
00:10:43,410 --> 00:10:45,160
That is all. Good luck...

123
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:49,220
The rest is indecipherable.

124
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:55,130
The signal was faint, but we made out
four keywords in this conversation:

125
00:10:55,130 --> 00:11:01,760
Princess Vivi; Straw Hat; 
written orders; and Mr. 0.

126
00:11:01,760 --> 00:11:05,100
Mr. 0? Could that be a code name?!

127
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:08,650
Perhaps he's connected 
to that suspicious swordsman

128
00:11:08,650 --> 00:11:10,230
we arrested back in Renaisse.

129
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:17,900
Mr.11
(Frontier Agent)
Baroque Works

130
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:13,180
Connected to him... Mr. 11?

131
00:11:13,180 --> 00:11:14,730
Yeah, seems like it.

132
00:11:14,730 --> 00:11:18,100
A criminal organization 
with numerical code names

133
00:11:18,100 --> 00:11:22,150
that sends written orders. Sound about right?

134
00:11:22,150 --> 00:11:26,220
Mr. 0? Criminal organization? 
Beats me.

135
00:11:26,220 --> 00:11:27,700
I've no time for riddles.

136
00:11:27,700 --> 00:11:32,230
Then why did we find a note 
with orders on it in your pocket?

137
00:11:32,230 --> 00:11:34,790
I thought I burned that letter!

138
00:11:34,790 --> 00:11:37,710
Th-That was... well...

139
00:11:37,710 --> 00:11:42,630
Strange. We didn't find 
anything in your pocket.

140
00:11:48,890 --> 00:11:50,600
Princess Vivi...

141
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:54,090
If memory serves, 
she's the princess of Arabasta.

142
00:11:54,090 --> 00:11:56,750
However, she's currently missing.

143
00:11:56,750 --> 00:12:01,480
Arabasta's in the 
midst of a coup, right?

144
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:04,400
Could this mysterious 
criminal organization

145
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:07,210
and the Straw Hats 
somehow be involved?

146
00:12:07,210 --> 00:12:08,790
Who knows?

147
00:12:08,790 --> 00:12:13,120
But this is the only clue leading us 
to the Straw Hats right now.

148
00:12:13,740 --> 00:12:15,710
So, we're going to–

149
00:12:15,710 --> 00:12:20,400
Yeah. Contact headquarters 
and requisition an eternal pose!

150
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:21,170
Yes, sir!

151
00:12:22,810 --> 00:12:28,720
We're going to Arabasta, 
the Kingdom of Sand!

152
00:12:39,650 --> 00:12:46,070
We had completely forgotten 
about the bounties on our heads!

153
00:12:46,070 --> 00:12:50,890
If it weren't for me, they would have 
never ventured to this island.

154
00:12:50,890 --> 00:12:51,700
Ow!

155
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:53,750
Don't give me that.

156
00:12:53,750 --> 00:12:57,180
Yeah, Vivi! Why're you 
so down in the dumps?

157
00:12:57,180 --> 00:12:58,200
Rice cracker?

158
00:12:58,200 --> 00:13:00,750
Wait, where'd those come from?

159
00:13:00,750 --> 00:13:03,530
All right! Time for a 
rice cracker party!

160
00:13:03,530 --> 00:13:05,760
Rice crackers aren't very exciting.

161
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:07,710
So then, raise a toast with 'em.

162
00:13:07,710 --> 00:13:10,190
See? Does anyone blame you?

163
00:13:10,190 --> 00:13:12,030
Cheers!

164
00:13:12,030 --> 00:13:15,190
Look! What a waste! Honestly!

165
00:13:15,190 --> 00:13:18,590
Seriously, you'll just 
ruin the food like that.

166
00:13:18,590 --> 00:13:21,970
What're you doing?! Give it here! 
Who said you could have mine?!

167
00:13:21,970 --> 00:13:25,570
– Give it back! It's mine!
– Says who?!

168
00:13:25,570 --> 00:13:27,110
What's wrong?

169
00:13:27,110 --> 00:13:29,070
Nothing. Just a bug.

170
00:13:29,760 --> 00:13:33,950
Still, it's no joke that the log takes one year to register the next island.

171
00:13:33,950 --> 00:13:37,420
You're right! It's no laughing matter!

172
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:42,300
You saved us. We would like 
to repay you in some way.

173
00:13:43,790 --> 00:13:47,260
Oh, in that case, 
you old guys should fix our log!

174
00:13:48,330 --> 00:13:52,220
I'm afraid even we aren't capable 
of helping with your log pose.

175
00:13:54,310 --> 00:13:58,190
Nami-san ! Vivi-chwan ! 
And the rest of you bums!

176
00:13:58,190 --> 00:14:00,690
Hey! Sanji!

177
00:14:01,650 --> 00:14:05,650
You're all safe! Thank goodness!

178
00:14:05,650 --> 00:14:10,570
Of course that flake shows up 
only after we need him.

179
00:14:12,580 --> 00:14:17,080
What in the hell?! Are you Mr. 3?!

180
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:20,700
Hey! How do you know about Mr. 3?

181
00:14:21,610 --> 00:14:22,590
Nami-san !

182
00:14:22,590 --> 00:14:25,050
How risqué you are!

183
00:14:25,050 --> 00:14:26,340
Wanna risk my fist?

184
00:14:26,340 --> 00:14:31,270
Allow me, Nami-san. 
You'll catch cold dressed like that.

185
00:14:31,270 --> 00:14:32,780
Please, wear this.

186
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:33,640
Thanks.

187
00:14:34,700 --> 00:14:39,600
All that aside, I just finished talking 
with Mr. 0 via transponder snail.

188
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:41,810
You talked to the boss?!

189
00:14:41,810 --> 00:14:46,530
Yeah. I found this weird hideout 
in the jungle, you see.

190
00:14:46,530 --> 00:14:55,080
He seemed to think I was Mr. 3, 
so I told him I eliminated everyone.

191
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:58,540
So that means he thinks we're dead?!

192
00:14:58,540 --> 00:15:01,620
Even if we've shaken those chasing us,

193
00:15:01,620 --> 00:15:04,510
we still can't go anywhere!

194
00:15:04,510 --> 00:15:08,560
Can't go anywhere? Do we still 
have business on this island?

195
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:11,800
I mean, I just got
a hold of this, too.

196
00:15:18,930 --> 00:15:20,060
Uh? What?

197
00:15:20,060 --> 00:15:23,400
It's an eternal pose to Arabasta!

198
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:26,800
– Hooray!
– Now we can set sail!

199
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:29,630
Hooray! Way to go, Sanji-kun !

200
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:34,300
Thank you, Sanji-san !

201
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:36,160
I'd almost lost hope!

202
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:41,620
No, no! It was my pleasure! 
I'm glad I could make you so happy!

203
00:15:41,620 --> 00:15:45,850
All right, everyone! 
Let's have a rice cracker party!

204
00:15:45,850 --> 00:15:47,720
Oh no, Luffy!

205
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:50,140
With only three left, 
we can't have a party!

206
00:15:50,140 --> 00:15:50,970
What?!

207
00:15:51,790 --> 00:15:54,590
All of that can be put on hold!

208
00:15:54,590 --> 00:15:57,810
Let's go, Captain! We can't waste a single second!

209
00:15:59,550 --> 00:16:00,930
Oh, yeah! Hey, you.

210
00:16:01,730 --> 00:16:04,900
You haven't forgotten
our hunting contest, I hope!

211
00:16:04,900 --> 00:16:10,110
Regarding that, I'm easily the winner.
I caught a rhino this big !

212
00:16:10,110 --> 00:16:13,790
A rhino? Is something 
like that edible?

213
00:16:13,790 --> 00:16:15,070
Of course!

214
00:16:15,670 --> 00:16:19,040
A hunting contest?

215
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:21,680
Somehow, this all sounds 
somehow familiar.

216
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:23,500
Yes.

217
00:16:25,690 --> 00:16:28,290
All right, round old guy 
and giant old guy!

218
00:16:28,290 --> 00:16:29,500
We're outta here!

219
00:16:31,550 --> 00:16:35,360
Oh? Well, you do seem anxious to leave.

220
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:37,410
Sad, but don't let us stop you.

221
00:16:37,410 --> 00:16:39,510
Best of wishes for your country.

222
00:16:39,510 --> 00:16:41,520
Yes! Thank you!

223
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:45,090
See ya! Don't die anymore!

224
00:16:45,770 --> 00:16:48,940
Master! I will visit Elbaf someday!

225
00:16:48,940 --> 00:16:52,000
You'll see. Mine's way bigger than yours.

226
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,400
You wish!

227
00:16:54,650 --> 00:16:56,990
I'm gonna be 
a brave warrior of the sea!

228
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:03,460
Our friends are setting sail.

229
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:08,500
Yes. We can't just sit here. 
There's a monster in the western sea.

230
00:17:09,270 --> 00:17:11,920
Dorry, how are your wounds?

231
00:17:12,660 --> 00:17:14,920
These? I'll live.

232
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:21,350
My axe and your sword 
are about finished.

233
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:25,770
Any regrets?

234
00:17:25,770 --> 00:17:30,200
Indeed. This axe has been my partner in battle for well over a century.

235
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:34,690
However, if it's to help them out, 
then it's worth it!

236
00:17:34,690 --> 00:17:37,200
That settles it.

237
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:49,700
See?! Mine's a lot 
bigger than yours!

238
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:51,800
Look closer! My lizard's enormous!

239
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:57,300
Are you blind or something?! 
My rhino's much more humongous!

240
00:17:57,300 --> 00:17:59,880
It doesn't matter! 
They both look delicious!

241
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:01,720
Mind your own business!

242
00:18:01,390 --> 00:18:01,720
Huh?

243
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:05,560
– Look! Mine's bigger!
– No, mine is!

244
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:08,650
And just how long do you two 
plan to keep at it?

245
00:18:08,650 --> 00:18:13,800
Just cut 'em up and stow 
what we can so we can set sail!

246
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:15,610
Yes, Nami-san !

247
00:18:15,610 --> 00:18:19,740
Hey, Usopp! I'm clearly 
the winner, right?!

248
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:21,040
I don't really care.

249
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:22,620
Can't you call it a draw?

250
00:18:22,620 --> 00:18:24,990
There are no draws in a challenge!

251
00:18:24,990 --> 00:18:26,620
Move your asses!

252
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:29,000
Right!

253
00:18:34,090 --> 00:18:36,380
Set sail!

254
00:18:40,090 --> 00:18:44,220
They said going straight will take us 
to the western end of the island.

255
00:18:44,220 --> 00:18:47,030
Hey. Is this all the meat 
we could carry?

256
00:18:47,030 --> 00:18:50,000
Use your head! 
We can't stow more than this.

257
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,060
Do you wanna sink the ship?!

258
00:18:58,370 --> 00:19:01,990
Look, it's the old guys! 
They came to see us off!

259
00:19:06,950 --> 00:19:09,910
Ahead is a great obstacle...

260
00:19:09,910 --> 00:19:14,880
...that prevents people who come 
to this island from reaching the next.

261
00:19:16,550 --> 00:19:21,160
You fought desperately 
to protect our pride.

262
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:24,510
Therefore, no matter the enemy 
that may rear its head...

263
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:31,060
...we will keep it from 
trampling your pride, friends!

264
00:19:33,350 --> 00:19:35,360
Have faith and keep straight!

265
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:38,740
No matter what happens, 
sail straight ahead!

266
00:19:39,820 --> 00:19:41,820
Got it!

267
00:19:41,820 --> 00:19:43,700
What's this about?

268
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:45,660
Wh-What's the word?

269
00:19:45,660 --> 00:19:48,620
We'll sail straight ahead, 
no matter what happens!

270
00:19:56,330 --> 00:19:57,740
We bid you farewell!

271
00:19:57,740 --> 00:19:59,440
Let's meet again someday.

272
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:00,550
Without fail.

273
00:20:00,550 --> 00:20:01,930
Look! Ahead!

274
00:20:08,580 --> 00:20:10,390
There you are, Island Gorger!

275
00:20:10,390 --> 00:20:14,350
You will make way, 
lest the pride of Elbaf fails us.

276
00:20:37,250 --> 00:20:38,130
Wha...?

277
00:20:38,130 --> 00:20:39,550
Something's appeared!

278
00:20:41,510 --> 00:20:44,470
What is this guy? A goldfish?

279
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:49,430
A g-giant goldfish?! 
Wh-Why does that sound familiar?!

280
00:20:49,430 --> 00:20:52,290
Work the rudder! Hurry! 
We're gonna get eaten!

281
00:20:52,290 --> 00:20:53,720
Usopp! Hurry!

282
00:20:53,720 --> 00:20:55,400
I... I can't!

283
00:20:55,400 --> 00:20:58,270
Go straight ahead! R-Right, Luffy?!

284
00:20:58,270 --> 00:21:00,610
Yeah! Of course!

285
00:21:06,570 --> 00:21:10,790
Don't be stupid! Laboon was 
one thing, but this is nothing like him!

286
00:21:10,790 --> 00:21:13,250
I know. Don't worry.

287
00:21:13,250 --> 00:21:15,920
Here, have the last rice cracker.

288
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:20,990
I don't want it! If we don't turn 
the ship, we're gonna be–

289
00:21:22,180 --> 00:21:24,010
Just give it up, Nami.

290
00:21:28,220 --> 00:21:31,390
Luffy! We can trust 
those guys, I take it?!

291
00:21:31,390 --> 00:21:32,220
Yeah!

292
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:35,690
Are you crazy?! Are we really 
sailing straight into that beast?!

293
00:21:35,690 --> 00:21:38,650
No! No turning back now!

294
00:21:47,660 --> 00:21:52,080
You've really grown, Island Gorger!
You monstrous goldfish!

295
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:56,040
His size isn't the only surprising thing.

296
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:58,690
This monster eats islands whole

297
00:21:58,690 --> 00:22:01,690
and poops them out in colossal turds.

298
00:22:01,690 --> 00:22:05,820
I recall one such floating 
dung heap was named Nihiland.

299
00:22:08,050 --> 00:22:13,010
We actually landed on it long ago,
mistaking it for an island!

300
00:22:13,010 --> 00:22:15,370
Today makes me 
nostalgic for adventure!

301
00:22:15,370 --> 00:22:18,480
As I watch that crew, 
I'm reminded of the old days!

302
00:22:22,440 --> 00:22:27,650
The one thing we've never pierced 
is the bloodstained snake!

303
00:22:28,690 --> 00:22:32,910
Behold! The mighty, legendary spear as taught only to those from Elbaf!

304
00:22:38,920 --> 00:22:41,380
Straight ahead! Straight ahead!

305
00:22:41,380 --> 00:22:44,630
What's the point?! 
We've already been eaten!

306
00:22:44,630 --> 00:22:46,960
Straight ahead! Straight ahead!

307
00:23:05,570 --> 00:23:08,000
Dominion!

308
00:23:09,320 --> 00:23:11,630
We're flying right out of it!

309
00:23:19,080 --> 00:23:22,540
Don't look back! 
We're keeping on straight ahead!

310
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:29,340
It's huge! So huge!

311
00:23:29,340 --> 00:23:33,280
They cut... the very sea itself...

312
00:23:33,280 --> 00:23:37,310
This is the strength of Elbaf warriors!

313
00:23:38,260 --> 00:23:40,990
It's incredible!

314
00:23:53,580 --> 00:23:54,780
Friends!

315
00:23:59,950 --> 00:24:02,000
Now go!

316
00:24:12,460 --> 00:24:16,380
Long ago, there was a group of 
ruffians on the sea...

317
00:24:16,380 --> 00:24:18,890
known as the Giant Warrior Pirates.

318
00:24:18,890 --> 00:24:21,970
The two pirate bosses,

319
00:24:21,970 --> 00:24:25,700
Brogy the Red Ogre 
and Dorry the Blue Ogre,

320
00:24:25,700 --> 00:24:27,360
stood unrivaled in might.

321
00:24:28,380 --> 00:24:32,000
Since ordinary people could not 
stand a chance against them,

322
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:34,290
they were left mostly unchecked.

323
00:24:34,290 --> 00:24:38,500
But they say that the one 
who finally put an end to them

324
00:24:38,500 --> 00:24:42,370
was a mere little girl.

325
00:24:45,040 --> 00:24:48,700
You see what our 
bosses caught today?!

326
00:24:48,700 --> 00:24:53,390
Yeah! It's all I can think about! 
What a day to be alive!

327
00:24:53,390 --> 00:24:58,890
Each one of 'em bagged 
an insanely huge sea king, after all!

328
00:24:58,890 --> 00:25:02,310
Even though we're Elbaf giants,

329
00:25:02,310 --> 00:25:05,210
nobody can take down those jumbo-sized monsters!

330
00:25:05,210 --> 00:25:07,600
Nobody but the bosses, that is!

331
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:09,110
Right, men?!

332
00:25:09,710 --> 00:25:12,860
– Yeah!
– You got that right!

333
00:25:15,030 --> 00:25:19,210
These ones are 
definitely the biggest yet!

334
00:25:21,400 --> 00:25:24,120
Yeah! Bigger than anything 
we've ever caught!

335
00:25:26,600 --> 00:25:28,920
So which one was bigger?

336
00:25:31,070 --> 00:25:33,180
– Which...
– ...one?

337
00:25:33,180 --> 00:25:36,340
Yeah! Who won the hunting contest?

338
00:25:41,050 --> 00:25:44,990
Look, Brogy! Mine is slightly bigger!

339
00:25:44,990 --> 00:25:48,420
Keep dreaming! Mine's a whole 
three centimeters longer!

340
00:25:48,420 --> 00:25:50,630
– Say what?!
– What?!

341
00:25:50,630 --> 00:25:53,780
Bosses! Please stop!

342
00:26:01,400 --> 00:26:07,210
Incidentally, Brogy. There's 
one thing I can't seem to remember.

343
00:26:07,210 --> 00:26:09,920
No, actually, same goes for me.

344
00:26:13,480 --> 00:26:14,880
The central mountain!

345
00:26:14,880 --> 00:26:19,260
No need to dwell on it! 
Let's settle this, once and for all!

346
00:26:19,260 --> 00:26:23,100
You're right! We'll sort things out afterward!
